---
import { SITE_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE } from "../consts";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<style>
			.hero {
				display: flex;
				gap: 3rem;
				background-color: #f2ede6;
				padding: 2em 3em;
				border-radius: 12px;
				box-shadow: var(--box-shadow);
			}
			.hero Image {
				border-radius: 12px;
				box-shadow: var(--box-shadow);
			}
			.hero .hero-cont {
				gap: 3rem;
				padding: 1rem 1em;
				font-size: 0.875em;
				color: rgb(var(--gray-dark));
			}
			h5 {
				color: #665433;
			}
			.hero .hero-cont {
				display: flex;
				flex: 1;
				flex-direction: column;
			}
			main {
				width: 100%;
				max-width: 960px;
			}
			p {
				font-size: 0.875em;
				color: rgb(var(--gray-dark));
			}
			.social-links {
				display: flex;
				gap: 1.5rem;
				margin-top: 1.5rem;
			}
			.social-links a {
				text-decoration: none;
			}
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		<div class="hero-cont">
			<h5>ABOUT JANET PILLAI</h5>
			<p>
				CEO and Founder of Multilayer Trade Corporation, (MLT Corp) a
				company that offers seamless vehicle hire, shuttle and
				accommodation solutions from inception to completion in the
				public, private corporate, tourist and maritime sectors. From
				2002-Present CEO and Founder of Multilayer Trade Corporation (
				MLT Corp Prop) trading as Articulate, a company focused on
				supporting companies with their marketing, PR and eventing
				logistics. From 2012-Present Chief Operating Officer at
				Inuversal Group Pty Ltd, a precision healthcare facility on the
				VNA Waterfront.
			</p>
		</div>
	</body>

	<h5 style="margin-top: 2em;">PROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE</h5>
	<p>
		Janet Pillai’s extensive business knowledge has built the capacity and
		infrastructure of the company to manage both mass and niche bespoke
		needs with both domestic and international clients. She has worked for
		academic institutions and governments and has achieved all her
		qualifications cum laude. She has been awarded the King Chavez Sparks
		Visiting Fellowship as well as a Visiting Fellowship to the Smithsonian
		Institution. Appointed as a visiting fellow at the University of Fort
		Hare. Janet was the lead in the Liberation Archives Project, which led
		to the establishment of the Liberation Archives building and
		reprository. She was also responsible for the aeration of the mirror
		archive at the Uniceristy of Michigan and the inclusion of the
		University in the Smitsonian South Africa delegation.
	</p>

	<p>
		Making the transition to government she managed the Arts, Culture and
		Heritage portfolio for the Western Cape Provincial Government until she
		established Multilayer Trade Corporation in 2002. MLT Corp and
		Articulate is a result driven companies which prides itself on good
		governance, sound turnaround time and service. The team has been
		handpicked and has had the benefit of Janet's mentorship and has grown
		with the company into positions they currently hold. Janet Pillai is
		active on the speaking circuit handling topics such as Transport,
		Tourism, Culture and Heritage, Wellness and Women's Development and
		Mentorship. She produces a podcast, focused on the tourism industry
		called Jetsetting with Janet.
	</p>

